author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**### Description:**\n\nWhen using GitHub Copilot in **AI Agent mode**, it incorrectly manages terminal sessions and the execution context. This results in:\n\n- Unnecessarily opening a new terminal even when one is already available.\n- Running commands in the **wrong directory**, often leading to command failures.\n\n---\n\n**Steps to Reproduce:**\n\n1. Enable **AI Agent mode** (via GitHub Copilot Chat or VS Code integration).\n2. Ask it to perform tasks like:\n   - `npm install`\n   - `next dev`\n3. Observe that:\n   - A new terminal is opened even if an active one exists.\n   - The command is executed in the wrong folder (e.g., root workspace instead of a subproject folder).\n\n---\n\n**Expected Behavior:**\n\n- Copilot should **reuse existing terminals** when possible.\n- It must **correctly detect the intended working directory** and navigate into it before running commands.\n- Ideally, it should **ask for confirmation** if directory context is ambiguous.\n\n---\n\n**Environment:**\n\n- **OS:** [e.g., Windows 11 / Ubuntu 22.04 / macOS Ventura]\n- **IDE:** VS Code [version, e.g., 1.90.0]\n- **Copilot Extension Version:** [use command palette → “Copilot: Help” → version info]\n- **Project Setup:** [Monorepo? Single project? Include if relevant]\n\n---\n\n**Additional Context:**\n\nThis issue breaks expected workflows, especially in multi-folder or monorepo environments. It creates unnecessary friction and errors during project setup and automation.\n\n","closed_by":{"login":"Tyriar","id":2193314,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTMzMTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2193314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tyriar","html_url":"https://github.com/Tyriar","fol